CALLED FROM WITHIN A PRINT LINE, DROPS THE CALLER'S LINE under the jitter. piCall prints a line whose middle item is a call
of piL, and piL prints a line of its own before it returns. PI-2 is the control: the same caller shape with a callee that
does not print (piQ), which agrees with the interpreted twin. The interpreted twin is this file with `jitter;` deleted
(pop.sh builds it); its PI-1 line is the intended value. Pinned at today's value: the jitted run prints PI-0 and NO PI-1
line at all.
